Here is a React bug to reproduce and fix, the stale-closure interval. Put this exact component in /workspace/fix-interval/src/Counter.jsx:

import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
export function Counter({ step }) {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  useEffect(() => {
    const id = setInterval(() => setCount(count + step), 1000);
    return () => clearInterval(id);
  }, []);
  return <span role="timer">{count}</span>;
}

First write a vitest plus @testing-library/react test with fake timers asserting that after advancing 3000ms with step 1 the timer reads 3, and watch it fail (it will read 1). Then fix using a functional update, and separately handle step changing mid-flight (rerender with step 5, advance, assert the math) either via a ref or effect deps, your choice, but the cleanup must not leak intervals: assert clearInterval call count with a spy. Keep the reproduction test as a regression. Full suite green.

